From here, the world looked different. The fence was lower than he had imagined. Beyond it, the neighbor’s yard was dark and tangled with weeds. A narrow path led between the houses, disappearing into shadow. Barnaby had heard the neighborhood cats talk about it in low, mysterious voices when they met on the fence at night. They called it the Alley of Whispers.

